    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d409">

                <pb facs="0466" n="458" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg458"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.733/31: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-05-25T14:00:00-04:00">May 25, 1939—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>193. Your 353, May 12, 4 p.m. You should acknowledge the receipt of the note of
                    May 9 from the Foreign Office and state in your note that a commission will be
                    issued to Mr. Irving N. Linnell as Consul General at Prague, Bohemia which will
                    be submitted with a formal application for his exequatur at an early date.</p>
                <p>You should also state orally when presenting your note that this action does not
                    indicate a change in this Government’s stated position with regard to
                        Czechoslovakia.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d409-f1"/></p>
                <p>The language of the final paragraph of the note of May 9 from the Foreign Office
                    indicates that exequaturs are not required for subordinate consular officers at
                    Prague. As Kennan has never had an exequatur, you may inquire orally whether an
                    exequatur will be required for him.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d409-f1" n="3" xml:id="d409-f1-content">
                <p>See Department of State, <hi rendition="#italic">Press Releases</hi>, March 18,
